# Pinned beagle ref — the FROZEN beagle commit gjoa builds against, COMPILER AND
# runtime. gjoa does NOT track live ~/code/beagle. This full object ID names an
# immutable checkout at ~/code/beagle/pins/<full-object-id>, with a same-name .pin
# sidecar naming Gjoa as its consumer. The build resolves the Beagle compiler from
# that checkout: .envrc sets PLTCOLLECTS through .beagle-pin-collects/beagle, and
# core.js is vendored from the same pin. CI checks out this object ID into its
# BEAGLE_PIN_ROOT override, so CI matches local. Preflight Gate M enforces exact
# full-HEAD equality. To advance, create the new detached content-addressed pin,
# update this file, then re-import and re-vendor; never re-point an existing pin.
# Canonical upstream: https://github.com/tompassarelli/beagle. This candidate is
# the newest revision with both upstream tests (run 30034827041) and native
# (run 30034828902) green; newer main was red when selected on 2026-07-27.
